本地定制把内联组合区改成「全文直写」，等于取消了上游的长度限制。受控编辑器
（Slate / Lexical / ProseMirror）必须把浏览器组合区映射回自己的文档模型，
一旦组合区跨过文本叶子或段落边界就抛
"Cannot resolve a Slate node from DOM node: [object HTMLSpanElement]"，
宿主输入框渲染中断。这就是「短句没事、长句必崩」的成因——是组合区长度，
不是输入框容量。

- ComposeLivePreedit 只流式尾部 160 字符（TailPreeditText），完整转写文本
  仍用于最终 commit，不再随说话时长增长
- enterBusyState 在已有转写文本时，把「识别中／正在后处理」追加在文字之后，
  而不是用状态行整体替换掉它
- 与上游 head...tail 折叠的区别：只留尾部，不吞句子中间

Verified: make -j (g++, C++20) 通过；ctest 47/47 通过
---
 src/addon/dbus/vinput_dbus.cpp | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/addon/dbus/vinput_dbus.cpp b/src/addon/dbus/vinput_dbus.cpp
index 5e57bec..754e01a 100644
--- a/src/addon/dbus/vinput_dbus.cpp
+++ b/src/addon/dbus/vinput_dbus.cpp
@@ -183,6 +183,34 @@ std::string LimitPreviewText(std::string_view text, int max_display_width) {
   return result;
 }
 
+// Streaming dictation is injected into the client as a composition region. Slate,
+// Lexical and ProseMirror map that region back onto their own document model and can
+// only do so while it stays inside a single text leaf: once a long dictation grows the
+// region past a leaf or paragraph boundary they throw
+// "Cannot resolve a Slate node from DOM node: [object HTMLSpanElement]" and the host
+// input box stops rendering. This is why short utterances are fine and long ones are
+// not - it is the length of the composition region, not the capacity of the text box.
+// Bound the region to the most recent speech, which is what the speaker is watching.
+constexpr size_t kMaxInlinePreeditChars = 160;
+
+std::string TailPreeditText(std::string_view text, size_t keep) {
+  std::u32string u32;
+  unicode::utf8::decode(text.data(), text.size(), u32);
+  if (u32.size() <= keep) {
+    return std::string(text);
+  }
+  constexpr std::string_view ellipsis = "...";
+  std::u32string ellipsis_u32;
+  unicode::utf8::decode(ellipsis.data(), ellipsis.size(), ellipsis_u32);
+  const std::u32string tail_u32 = u32.substr(u32.size() - keep);
+  std::string result;
+  unicode::utf8::encode(ellipsis_u32.data(), ellipsis_u32.size(), result);
+  std::string tail_str;
+  unicode::utf8::encode(tail_u32.data(), tail_u32.size(), tail_str);
+  result.append(tail_str);
+  return result;
+}
+
 std::string ComposeLivePreedit(const std::string& transcript_text, const std::string& fallback_text,
                                int max_display_width = 0) {
   (void)max_display_width;
@@ -190,9 +218,10 @@ std::string ComposeLivePreedit(const std::string& transcript_text, const std::st
     return fallback_text;
   }
 
-  // Never fold or swallow spoken text into "head...tail" - streaming preedit flows
-  // directly into the client input box, which wraps naturally across multiple lines.
-  return transcript_text;
+  // Keep the whole utterance for the final commit, but only stream a bounded tail
+  // inline. Folding into "head...tail" hides the middle of the sentence; growing
+  // without a bound breaks controlled editors.
+  return TailPreeditText(transcript_text, kMaxInlinePreeditChars);
 }
 
 std::string RenderMethodCallFailure(std::string_view error_name, std::string_view error_message,
@@ -507,7 +536,20 @@ void VinputEngine::enterBusyState(fcitx::InputContext* ic, bool command_mode,
   session_->command_mode = command_mode;
   session_->raw_prev = effective_raw_prev;
   status_ic_ = ic;
-  if (!session_->raw_prev) {
+  const bool has_transcript = !command_mode && !session_->transcript_text.empty();
+  if (has_transcript) {
+    // Dictation must never replace text that is already on screen with a bare
+    // status line. Both "... Recognizing ..." and "... Postprocessing ..." are
+    // appended behind the transcript instead of wiping it - replacing it is what
+    // made the text look deleted the moment the voice key was released.
+    const auto transcript =
+        TailPreeditText(session_->transcript_text, kMaxInlinePreeditChars);
+    updateVoicePresentation(ic, transcript + "  " + preedit_text,
+                            session_->raw_prev
+                                ? LimitPreviewText(session_->transcript_text,
+                                                   max_streaming_display_width_)
+                                : std::string{});
+  } else if (!session_->raw_prev) {
     updateVoicePresentation(ic, preedit_text);
   } else if (postprocessing && !session_->transcript_text.empty()) {
     const auto transcript =
